      "problem": "If $\\log_2(3)=k$ and $\\log_2(x)=p,$ what is the value of $\\log_2(3x)?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the product rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\log_n a + \\log_n b = \\log_n(ab)\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{2}⁡(3x) & ={log}_{2}⁡3+{log}_{2}⁡x \\\\  & =k+p.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
